### Project-specific ###
# Trained policy checkpoints (binary, per-run artifacts -- not source).
# Previously untracked-but-committed history already bloated .git to ~142MB;
# this stops it from growing further. Existing large blobs stay in history
# unless someone runs a filter-repo pass separately.
#
# `checkpoints/*`, NOT `checkpoints/` -- git cannot re-include anything under a
# directory that is itself excluded, so the directory has to stay visible for
# the exception below to be reachable at all. Consequence: this is now anchored
# to the repo root, so a nested copy (cluster/cluster/checkpoints/, as landed
# once via scp) is NOT covered any more. Watch for that in `git status`.
checkpoints/*
# EXCEPTION, 2026-08-25: ONE checkpoint is tracked on purpose, because scp to
# the cluster would not work and git pull was the way to get it there. It is
# the 50M lidar-only Saute run that cluster/ant_minefield_lidar_resume100M.sbatch
# resumes from -- 6.4 MB, 9 files.
#
# THIS IS PERMANENT. Deleting it later shrinks the working tree but not .git;
# the blob stays in history unless someone runs a filter-repo pass. Do not use
# this as a precedent for the other checkpoints -- the rule above exists
# because that habit already took .git to ~142 MB.
#
# Each level has to be re-included in turn; a single negation of the leaf does
# not work, because git stops descending at the first excluded parent.
!checkpoints/ant_minefield_saute500_lidar_wide/
checkpoints/ant_minefield_saute500_lidar_wide/*
!checkpoints/ant_minefield_saute500_lidar_wide/000050176000/
# Training/eval logs (logs/). Per-run artifacts like checkpoints, not source.
# NOTE: these are the only record of what a run actually did -- reward curves,
# episode lengths, crash exit codes -- and being ignored they exist on ONE
# machine. Copy anything you intend to cite in a writeup somewhere durable.
cluster/download.md
logs/
# Vast.ai instance id (per-rental, machine-local)
cluster/vast/.instance
